n Historical Reserve. It is located on the southwestern side of Heavitree Gap in Alice Springs in the Northern Territory of Australia.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Heavitree Gap Police Station","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Heavitree_Gap_Police_Station.jpg/1280px-Heavitree_Gap_Police_Station.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Heavitree_Gap_Police_Station.jpg/500px-Heavitree_Gap_Police_Station.jpg","w":1200,"h":902,"author":"Michaeljbarritt","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heavitree_Gap_Police_Station.jpg"}},{"id":"alice_springs_adelaide_house","areaId":"alice_springs","name":"Adelaide House","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-23.6996,"lng":133.88256},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"alice_springs_adelaide_house","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":59,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["adelaidehouse","alicesprings"],"summary":"The first stone building in Alice, on the Todd Mall and well worth a visit if only for the absolutely amazing early air-conditioning system. Really cool display of old communications technology, like the bike-powered communications radio. Run by a couple old women who serve tea - an excellent place to have a sit-down. Nice and quiet.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Alice Springs","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/Mapillary_%28UouhNTTfL16-Jb7BRN_gAQ%29_%28bob3bob3%29_2018-08-10_09H42M30S000.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/Mapillary_%28UouhNTTfL16-Jb7BRN_gAQ%29_%28bob3bob3%29_2018-08-10_09H42M30S000.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"bob3bob3","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapillary_